He could be put in the same situation a hundred times, and he would still make the same decisions each time. It was who he was. He wasn’t a man of virtue and integrity like Dr. Ettman and his son. He pretended to be one while

in the public eye, but when he was alone with Layla, even pretending to be virtuous was impossible for him.
