His final moments…?

When she heard that phrase, the tears stopped falling from her eyes, and she became aware of a truth that she desperately wanted to deny. Perhaps she had been vaguely aware of this truth the moment she had first entered the hospital room and seen him.
Gasping like a choking person, she staggered back to the bedside. Smiling and crying at once, she looked at Uncle Bill.







“You always said that you knew I would become an outstanding adult. You still think so, right? You still believe in me?”
Does she really have to ask?
Bill almost burst into laughter at Layla’s obvious question. Instead, however, all that came out as a series of burning coughs, after which some sort of hot liquid started seeping out of his mouth.
