The plan had to remain an absolute secret. All three men understood this without anyone having to state it explicitly. They were planning to violate a direct order from their commander during wartime. This was a serious crime. If they were caught, even a high-ranking aristocrat like Duke Herhardt would not be able to escape punishment.
