The look on Riette’s face shifted from exasperation to mild pity. “If this is how things were going to end up, I would’ve rather-”
Riette’s sentence was cut off by a loud explosion. Matthias reflexively sprung to his feet and ran to the window to open the curtain. Meanwhile, an

even closer explosion shook the entire building. “It’s an air raid! An enemy air raid!”
The air-raid siren started ringing, along with an amplified voice ordering everyone to take cover. The quiet hotel transformed into a noisy pandemonium in an instant. The departure time for the ambulance that Kyle Ettman would be driving was about an hour away.
